A||N||14||grinthock||What's your Wax Secret?||||5||
Z||000000||grinthock||04-15-2001||10:34 AM||||Well everyone, here is spring/summer and alot of your are going to be out waxin your cars, What I wnat to know is what is everyone's method?   <P>Reply to this post and let everyone know<P>1) What steps do you take?<BR>2)  What products do you use?<BR>3)  Any secrets or recipes?<P><BR>Thanks.   <BR>Justin||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||04-15-2001||10:42 AM||||Meguire's Deep Crystal 3-step system.<BR>Cleaner = Once every spring<BR>Polish = Once every 6 months<BR>Wax = Once a month<P>(Mostly Original Paint  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  )<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSC00007_1.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||04-15-2001||11:16 AM||||How to care for the paint depends a lot on location. Ive seen clearcoats that have been waxed and waxed-but peeling in a few years anyway. Also seen cars that are rarely washed with the paint in good shape. 90% of keeping it looking good is just simple cleaning. I personally dont wax any of my cars.  I just keep them washed. Ill rub out with compound maybe once a year. I prefer to use polishes rather than wax. I like Turtle Wax Swirl Remover best. You can put it on as often as you want, takes out all the minor scratches that even a terry towel leave. So it always has a wet look. Wax will leave a buildup after so many applications and dull the finish and will even turn whites to eggshell color. Wax will also make paint bead, which used to be a good thing. But now with clearcoats, unless you dry it off all those little drops are like tiny magnifying lenses burning holes in the clear. So its preferable to have whats called 'sheeting' where all the water just runs off, no beading. Look at your car sometime after its rained and dried. all those spots contain minerals eating the paint and they wont come off unless you wipe them with a damp or wet towel. The wax dont stop them. The only real time Id use a good wax is if I was in an area with lots of tree sap, birds,or airborne chemicals.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||sjp777||04-15-2001||11:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Meguire's Deep Crystal 3-step system.<BR>Cleaner = Once every spring<BR>Polish = Once every 6 months<BR>Wax = Once a month<P>(Mostly Original Paint   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  )<P> <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That is the hot ticket<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||14
