Z||000008||Master_Sushi||04-15-2001||01:02 PM||||I bought a cheap 30$ buffer at kmart last week. It spins somewhat slowly and vibrates, but it seems to do a nice job. I just use mothers wax with the 30$ orbital buffer and it works really nicely. My fiero dosent have to many miles so I dont have many scratches, but the small scratches it seems to take out. My white paint comes out very bright and shiney after a good buffing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I really recomend a cheap buffer, they seem to work better then a hand wax. Oh, and as long as its not a high speed one, you dont really have to worry about screwing your paint up with it.||||reg||14
Z||000009||mgbringo||04-15-2001||01:38 PM||||Zaino Brothers is the only way to go.  I have switched from Mequires to Zaino and am really impressed.  Not sold in stores, have to order it.  Costs more and is more work but worth it.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.zainobros.com" TARGET=_blank>www.zainobros.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||kslish||04-15-2001||03:13 PM||||Been using my own three step system for a while just because I picked up each of them dirt cheap at the local Big Lots.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>Step 1:<BR>Liquid Crystal Polish - Do they even still make this stuff?  It used to be like $15 a bottle in stores, but fortunately I stocked up when I got it for $5/bottle.  It's great stuff...not abrasive at all yet it removes surface contaminants and leaves a great shine.  <P>Step 2:<BR>Mother's Sealer and Glaze - Removes the swirl marks and helps hide some of the deaper scratches.<P>Step 3:<BR>Meguire's Deep Crystal Pure Carnuba Wax - Seems to help protect the surface longer and the shine holds up better than if I skip this step due to lack of time.  <P>My car unfortunately sleeps outside, so I have to keep wax on it.<P>I perform the ritual around three times a year....usually right before a major show.  I get complements on the shine (and it's not a clearcoat).  <P> <IMG SRC="http://westpennfiero.onestop.net/FOCOA1.jpg"> <P>(mine is the red one closest to the camera)<P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||grinthock||04-15-2001||03:57 PM||||WOW!  After hearing all this good stuff about that 3 step system I am gonna go out and get some!  Gotta buy a buffer first, but that's fine!||||reg||7
Z||000012||RossT||04-15-2001||05:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mgbringo:<BR><B>Zaino Brothers is the only way to go.  I have switched from Mequires to Zaino and am really impressed.  Not sold in stores, have to order it.  Costs more and is more work but worth it.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.zainobros.com" TARGET=_blank>www.zainobros.com</A> <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I aslo use zaino!!! a little pricey but a little goes a long long way.<P>BTW i will be in fargo next week 4/19,20,21,22 for a convention.  I am not bringing the fiero (bringing the family instead) but I would like to see yours.  I am staying at the New Ramada tower in SW Fargo.  The one with the water slide.  Let me know if we can work something out!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Fformula88||04-15-2001||08:35 PM||||I usually use the 3 step system about once a year.  Thats when I start to notice swirls in the paint from my constant washing and drying  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I try to wax the car at least once a month, but I use Nu-Finish.  I've also used Maguires, and haven't noticed much of a difference.  The Nu removes tar a little better for me, and with my areas constant road work all summer I prefer the Nu.  Otherwise, just I just try and keep it clean and dust/dirt free.||||reg||1
Z||000014||grinthock||04-16-2001||05:47 PM||||Well have ot say, used that 3-step system today but shey should have said<P>Step 1 - Good shine<P>Step 2 - Great Shine<P>Step 3 - SHOW Shine<P>because in all honesty it looked better and better as I went to it, took me a hell of a long time but it was worth it||||reg||4
